 ## Overview
-`GaussianRasterizationSettings` is a configuration structure (typically a `NamedTuple` or struct) that encapsulates the camera parameters, scene constraints, and rendering flags required to invoke the differentiable 3D Gaussian rasterizer [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem of translating high-level camera definitions (Field of View, view/projection matrices) and scene properties into the specific numerical formats expected by the underlying CUDA kernel [S1, unofficial]. It differs from the rasterizer itself by handling the setup of state and memory layout rather than the pixel-wise projection and blending logic [S1, unofficial].
+`GaussianRasterizationSettings` is a configuration structure (typically a `NamedTuple` or struct) that encapsulates camera parameters, scene constraints, and rendering flags required to invoke the differentiable 3D/4D Gaussian rasterizer [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem of translating high-level camera definitions (Field of View, view/projection matrices) and scene properties into the specific numerical formats expected by the underlying CUDA kernel [S1, unofficial]. It differs from the rasterizer itself by handling the setup of state and memory layout rather than the pixel-wise projection and blending logic [S1, unofficial].
 
